WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.909
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:15.669
Unit twenty-four: Job Interviews. Today you will talk about experience with the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:18.610
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.741
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.492
Interview.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.597
Interview means a meeting where an employer asks you questions.

8
00:00:29.183 --> 00:00:31.369
My first interview is on Monday.

9
00:00:31.983 --> 00:00:34.485
Your turn. Say: Interview.

10
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:38.416
Interview.

11
00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.081
Employer.

12
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.128
Employer means a person or company that gives jobs.

13
00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:46.635
The employer liked my answers.

14
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.647
Your turn. Say: Employer.

15
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.443
Employer.

16
00:00:54.183 --> 00:00:55.324
Skills.

17
00:00:56.317 --> 00:00:58.444
Skills means things you can do well.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.759
List your skills on your resume.

19
00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.968
Your turn. Say: Skills.

20
00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:07.730
Skills.

21
00:01:08.483 --> 00:01:09.728
Experience.

22
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:13.332
Experience means what you learn by doing.

23
00:01:13.917 --> 00:01:16.032
I have some experience with children.

24
00:01:16.617 --> 00:01:19.594
Your turn. Say: Experience.

25
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:23.643
Experience.

26
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:25.628
Qualification.

27
00:01:26.617 --> 00:01:30.009
Qualification means a certificate or exam you have passed.

28
00:01:30.617 --> 00:01:33.023
A computer qualification helps.

29
00:01:33.617 --> 00:01:36.350
Your turn. Say: Qualification.

30
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.410
Qualification.

31
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.116
Confident.

32
00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:45.035
Confident means sure of yourself.

33
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:47.441
Smile and look confident.

34
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.551
Your turn. Say: Confident.

35
00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.343
Confident.

36
00:01:55.083 --> 00:01:55.968
Prepare.

37
00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.518
Prepare means to get ready.

38
00:01:59.117 --> 00:02:01.476
Prepare answers to common questions.

39
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.643
Your turn. Say: Prepare.

40
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.327
Prepare.

41
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:10.073
Impression.

42
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:13.768
Impression means the feeling people get about you.

43
00:02:14.383 --> 00:02:16.081
Make a good first impression.

44
00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:19.405
Your turn. Say: Impression.

45
00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.372
Impression.

46
00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:27.620
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.483 --> 00:02:31.412
Visal, how would you prepare for a job interview?

48
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:35.793
I would research the employer and practise my answers.

49
00:02:36.883 --> 00:02:38.894
What experience could you talk about?

50
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:45.492
I have worked in a team on a school project. I have volunteered at a library.

51
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:48.374
What about first impressions?

52
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:52.818
I'd dress neatly, smile and look confident.

53
00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:55.792
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:56.650 --> 00:03:00.043
Grammar focus: Present perfect for experience.

55
00:03:00.343 --> 00:03:01.483
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:03.591
I have worked in a team.

57
00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.297
I have volunteered at a library.

58
00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:08.951
She has led a student club.

59
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:13.537
Use the present perfect to talk about experience without saying when.

60
00:03:14.283 --> 00:03:17.667
Be careful! Don't say: I have volunteer at a library.

61
00:03:19.633 --> 00:03:22.411
Say: I have volunteered at a library.

62
00:03:22.711 --> 00:03:25.059
After 'have', use the past participle.

63
00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:28.542
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:30.729
Ready for the Interview.

65
00:03:31.029 --> 00:03:33.447
Before a job interview, prepare well.

66
00:03:34.433 --> 00:03:37.524
The employer wants to know your skills and experience.

67
00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:41.810
Say what you have done, for example: I have worked in a team.

68
00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.380
Show your qualifications and be confident.

69
00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:48.726
Be polite and make a good first impression.

70
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:53.928
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:54.783 --> 00:03:56.435
I have blank at a library.

72
00:03:56.735 --> 00:04:00.725
A, volunteered. B, volunteer. C, volunteering.

73
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.591
The answer is A: volunteered.

74
00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.806
A person or company that gives jobs is an blank.

75
00:04:11.106 --> 00:04:14.887
A, employer. B, employee. C, interview.

76
00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:20.549
The answer is A: employer.

77
00:04:21.683 --> 00:04:24.020
The feeling people get about you is an blank.

78
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:28.728
A, impression. B, experience. C, qualification.

79
00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:34.498
The answer is A: impression.

80
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.840
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:39.683 --> 00:04:41.950
How would you prepare for a job interview?

82
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.250
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:52.550 --> 00:05:01.553
I would research the company and practise my answers. I would say, 'I have worked in a team and I have volunteered,' and I would be confident and polite.

84
00:05:01.853 --> 00:05:04.073
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:04.983 --> 00:05:09.644
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect for experience.

86
00:05:09.944 --> 00:05:15.104
Today's value is professionalism. Be prepared, polite and reliable in everything you do.

87
00:05:15.404 --> 00:05:18.440
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

88
00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.031
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

